Yes. I went back through the product-reset decisions and everything we've discussed since then, rather than just the last couple of conversations.

The good news is: a lot has already been finalized. But I would not call V2 100% ready until you check a few specific items.

What I found

🔴 1. Wallet connection — make sure it's removed

We explicitly decided that wallet connection is NOT part of the current onboarding/dashboard.

Wallet infrastructure can remain for future:

verified accounts

opportunities

rewards

payouts

credentials


But the current user experience should not require connecting a wallet.

If wallet connection is still visible anywhere in V2 onboarding/dashboard, remove it.


---

🔴 2. V2 score — verify the five dimensions

The V2 score was frozen around these five dimensions:

1. Process


2. Risk


3. Execution


4. Behavior


5. Learning & Consistency



The score should be off-chain.

Also, we specifically wanted to avoid a score that can be gamed through simple self-reporting. It should eventually consider multiple signals, consistency, contradictions and improvement over time.

So check whether the current V2 actually reflects these five dimensions.


---

🔴 3. The core loop needs to remain intact

We defined the KAIZEN loop as:

PLAN → TRADE → REFLECT → ANALYZE → IMPROVE → REPEAT

Make sure V2 still communicates and supports this loop.

That is more important than adding another feature.


---

🟠 4. AI functions — verify the agreed scope

The initial AI scope was finalized as:

Pattern Detection & Explanation

Personalized Coaching

Performance Analysis

Mistake Identification

Reflection

Progress Feedback

Context-Aware Conversation

Explaining the KAIZEN Score


Improvement Recommendations and Goal Guidance were deliberately deferred.

So if V2 currently contains those deferred functions, I'd remove/hide them rather than pretending they're ready.


---

🔴 5. Charting is now the biggest architectural item

This one has evolved significantly since the reset.

We decided that KAIZEN's chart cannot just be:

> Entry → SL → TP.



The eventual chart needs to support actual market study:

timeframes

drawings

indicators

support/resistance

analysis

thesis

replay

backtesting/simulation

chart activity

connection between chart analysis and trade

connection between trade and reflection


And importantly:

> Journaling alone isn't enough.



We want KAIZEN to understand how the trader studied the market and arrived at the decision.

However, I would NOT make the full chart a V2 launch blocker now.

TradingView is still handling the Advanced Charts request, while we've already decided the native chart will eventually be KAIZEN-owned.


---

🟠 6. Replay/backtesting

We also established that replay should eventually be a KAIZEN-owned feature, rather than depending on TradingView.

And you wanted replay to be free.

If V2 currently advertises replay/backtesting but doesn't actually work, don't market it as available yet.


---

🟠 7. Trader profile / "Personal KAIZEN"

This was one of the bigger product ideas from the reset.

KAIZEN shouldn't simply know:

> "You lost a trade."



It should eventually understand:

> "This is how you trade, these are your recurring behaviours, these are the mistakes you repeatedly make, and this is how you're changing."



That requires the underlying trader profile/data model.

If you've already implemented the profile foundation, good.

If not, the architecture should at least be designed now, even if the full intelligence comes later.


---

🟠 8. Trading-plan / rules data

We also identified the need for structured information about a trader's:

trading rules

strategy/system

risk rules

planned behaviour


Otherwise KAIZEN can't properly distinguish:

> "You lost."



from:

> "You broke your own rule and that's part of a recurring pattern."



This is important for the Behavior and Process dimensions of the score.


---

🟢 9. Survey — this part is effectively done

You wanted real trader feedback before rebuilding.

You've now got enough responses to make the V2 decision, and you've finalized the direction.

We also added the useful question around:

> “When reviewing a trade, what do you currently use to analyze your decision?”



That was specifically intended to determine whether traders are actually studying/analyzing charts rather than simply logging trades.

So I wouldn't hold V2 for more survey responses.


---

🟢 10. Product direction is now much clearer

One major change we've made is that KAIZEN isn't being positioned as simply:

AI + Trading Journal.

The direction is now closer to:

Chart analysis → decision → execution → reflection → behavioural understanding → improvement.

And eventually the chart itself becomes a major source of behavioural intelligence.

That's a significant product reset.


